/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/README.md:304:- local mode reads policy from root `spawn`; remote mode reads `remote.spawn`, falling back to root `spawn` when `remote.spawn` is missing or `null`. Both locations use the identical surface: `enabled` defaults to `true`, `max_parallel` defaults to `20`, optional `preferred_agentic_system`, optional UTC `schedule`, legacy `preferred_agent`, default-on `launch_composition.enabled`, and optional per-agent `ceilings` with role overrides. Spawn providers are `agy`, `claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `muse`, and `qwen`. The canonical provider system is a tagged union: `{"exclusive":"agy"}` pins one provider, while `{"mixed":["agy","codex"]}` permits the normalized set. `schedule.windows[]` uses start-inclusive/end-exclusive `start_utc` / `end_utc` values in `HH:MM` and a per-window `preferred_agentic_system`; later-to-earlier bounds cross midnight (for example `17:00` to `03:00`). Windows must be disjoint. An active window replaces the base provider system, while gaps use the base system or unrestricted runtime affinity when no base exists. An explicit `--agent` and any registered requested model must belong to the active set; violations are refused before side effects with the allowed providers and a retry step. The selected provider's ceiling applies afterward. `max_parallel` schedules runners only within one client work directory; it is not a remote-board or cross-client limit. `project_config().spawn.config_key_prefix` names the effective source, `project_config().spawn.preferred_agentic_system` reports the currently effective mode/set/provenance, `project_config().spawn.schedule` reports UTC windows plus the active window, and `project_config().spawn.launch_composition.config_key` names the active composition field. `model_criterion: equal` pins an exact model, `less_or_equal` clamps above a provider-local rank, and `greater_or_equal` raises below it. Role keys and `--role` values are trimmed and case-folded before lookup; `coordinator` shares the `orchestrator` policy identity, while path-like or unknown roles fail closed before selection. Ordered criteria require a one-line `--selection-rationale`; an adjusted pair additionally requires exact `--ack-resolved <model>/<effort>` after re-evaluation with fresh rationale text.
