/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/skill-project-management/docs/remote-board-operations.md:90:- `remote.spawn` has the same policy surface and preflight enforcement as local root `spawn`: `enabled`, `max_parallel`, canonical `preferred_agentic_system` (`exclusive` or `mixed`), optional disjoint UTC `schedule.windows`, legacy `preferred_agent`, default-on `launch_composition.enabled`, versioned agent ceilings, and role overrides. An active schedule window replaces the base provider system; provider membership is enforced before remote task lookup or local runner side effects. Existing remote profiles with a missing or `null` `remote.spawn` retain the complete root `spawn` object as a migration fallback; a present remote object defaults launch composition on when the field is omitted. In v3, exact membership in the admitted `(model, effort)` pair set is the sole admission authority and the optional `resolution_model` is the only model fallback. That pair set is declared by exactly one of `allowed_models` or `entries` per provider; neither key is itself the authority, and `project_config()` reports the resolved set as `admitted_pairs`. Capability `PolicyRank` never changes the set: ordered entries consult it at parse time only against an operator-approved `entries_expansion_digest`.
