+# TASK-260830-1srcgk developer outcome
+
+## Delivered scope
+
+- `task-board.config.json`: set `spawn.max_parallel` to `1` and migrated the Codex ceiling to `spawn-policy-v4` with one exact admitted pair, `gpt-5.6-sol/high`.
+- `docs/spawn-policy.md`: changed every producer, reviewer, architecture-producer, and config example from medium to high; documented a fresh serial reviewer and the exact-pair fail-closed bound.
+- `.spec/goal-macos-v1.md`: aligned the execution model with primary goal revision 8: Sol/high for the primary, every producer/rework owner, and every fresh reviewer, with `max_parallel 1`.
+- No product runtime, VPN activation, NetworkExtension state, routing, DNS, or system networking was touched.
+
+## Effective preflights and negative evidence
+
+Both worktree-effective preflights used `TASK_BOARD_CONFIG=$PWD/task-board.config.json` and exited 0. Developer and reviewer each resolved:
+
+- provider: Codex only;
+- context profile: lite;
+- `max_parallel: 1`;
+- contract: `spawn-policy-v4`;
+- admitted pairs: exactly `gpt-5.6-sol:high` (digest `sha256:e2768012d97d2577f6b5536d3940547f56803113beb08e062d8f45a39d801709`).
+
+Negative probes exercised the production `task-board spawn` admission call site with a valid-shaped nonexistent task ID and `gpt-5.6-sol/medium`, so a broken gate could reach task lookup but could not create or mutate a real task. Developer and reviewer probes both exited 1 with typed `spawn_no_supported_effort_under_ceiling`; log assertions exited 0. The rejected pair therefore cannot be routed under the replacement policy.
+
+Evidence:
+
+- `developer-preflight.log` — SHA-256 `bade23955c20487ab649d3447eac5a1cd3714a0dfe4ef86fdfd67d0e3d0494d9`
+- `reviewer-preflight.log` — SHA-256 `78450552a32478f1ed62b6d2ec35bd86d97ae47bea48883b35b999a2364aa8a8`
+- developer/reviewer medium negative logs — SHA-256 `112614d0f094ce3679ea74c29fc655cba3c8a7f97ff2d0f012f9bf613acb461b`
+
+## Goal and drift checks
+
+- `task-board goal get` exited 0 and reported `PRIMARY-GOAL-260728-3lhfz3 revision 8`, including one Sol/high worker, lite context, `max_parallel 1`, and producer then fresh reviewer serially.
+- JSON/config assertions exited 0.
+- Focused canonical drift scan exited 0: no medium or `max_parallel 3` policy remains in the three scoped files; all three spawn examples use high.
+- `git diff --check` exited 0. The scoped diff contains only the three files above. Existing unrelated dirty changes in `LOGBOOK.md`, `README.md`, the CI trust-boundary diagram/artifact, and its contract document were preserved and not edited or staged by this task.
+- Product build was intentionally not run because the delta is orchestration JSON/Markdown only; effective config parsing, positive preflights, negative admission probes, drift assertions, and diff checks are the relevant validation surface.
+
